Q('l07', mk.long({ marks: 10, stem: 'An imagined school club hires a bus for a trip for ₹$1200$, the cost to be shared equally by the members who go. Five members drop out, and each of the others has to pay ₹$20$ more.\n(a) Taking $x$ as the number of members who first planned to go, show that $x^2 - 5x - 300 = 0$.\n(b) Solve the equation and find how many members actually went on the trip.\n(c) Find the share of each member who went. Had four more members joined the original group instead, how much less would each have paid than in the original plan?', model: J([r`**(a)** Planned share ₹$\dfrac{1200}{x}$; actual share ₹$\dfrac{1200}{x - 5}$, which is ₹$20$ more.`, ...wl07.md.slice(0, 4), r`**(b)**`, ...wl07.md.slice(4), r`A number of members cannot be negative, so $x = 20$ planned to go and $20 - 5 = 15$ members went.`, `**(c)** Each member who went paid ${wl07c.md[0]} rupees, that is ₹$80$.`, `In the original plan each would have paid ${wl07c.md[1]} rupees; with $24$ members, ${wl07c.md[2]} rupees. So each would have paid ${wl07c.md[3]} rupees less, that is ₹$10$ less.`]), sol: 'Write each share as total cost over the number of members; the difference is ₹20. Reject the negative count.', scheme: [['(a) both shares', 1], ['(a) equation', 1], ['(a) simplified', 1], ['(b) factorised', 1], ['(b) x = 20 (−15 rejected)', 1], ['(b) 15 went', 1], ['(c) ₹80', 1], ['(c) ₹60', 1], ['(c) ₹50', 1], ['(c) ₹10 less', 1]], d: 3, c: 'application', t: [4], time: 720 }), (C) => { wl07.verify(C); wl07c.verify(C); C.assert(1200 / 15 - 1200 / 20 === 20, 'story'); C.model([20, 15, 80, 60, 50, 10]); });

